WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.665
No court can force you to

2
00:00:01.665 --> 00:00:03.194
perform a Fundamental Duty.

3
00:00:03.394 --> 00:00:05.442
So why do judges keep citing them?

4
00:00:05.942 --> 00:00:08.040
Article 51A lists the duties

5
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.313
of every citizen.

6
00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:11.606
The 42nd Amendment added

7
00:00:11.606 --> 00:00:13.507
ten of them, in 1976.

8
00:00:13.907 --> 00:00:16.180
The 86th Amendment, in 2002,

9
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.641
added an eleventh:

10
00:00:17.761 --> 00:00:19.437
parents and guardians must

11
00:00:19.437 --> 00:00:21.307
provide chances for education

12
00:00:21.307 --> 00:00:23.435
to children aged six to fourteen.

13
00:00:23.885 --> 00:00:25.490
The duties can't be enforced

14
00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:26.637
directly by a court.

15
00:00:27.037 --> 00:00:28.776
But in the AIIMS Students'

16
00:00:28.776 --> 00:00:30.715
Union case, the Supreme Court

17
00:00:30.715 --> 00:00:32.320
called them as important

18
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:32.989
as rights,

19
00:00:33.109 --> 00:00:34.987
and a guide to interpreting laws.

20
00:00:35.437 --> 00:00:37.077
Courts have also read the

21
00:00:37.077 --> 00:00:39.109
duty to protect the environment

22
00:00:39.109 --> 00:00:40.749
into environmental cases.

23
00:00:41.199 --> 00:00:42.265
Not a command.

24
00:00:42.465 --> 00:00:43.425
A lens.

25
00:00:43.925 --> 00:00:44.800
Your turn.

26
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.970
Which amendment added Article

27
00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:48.641
51A to the Constitution?
